  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `fn[fingerprint]` in `GraphWithChangingEdges`'s `Contents` impl is a valid coverage exception.\n\n- **Placement:** It is a fenced citation with commentary on an explicit function that has a body. That is a form the built-in permits.\n- **Reason is substantive:** The commentary says `Contents` requires `fingerprint`, but this regression observes only the outgoing-edge selection. It also says no node contents are read, so a content fingerprint would contradict the asserted selection-only dependencies. This is a real reason, not just difficulty.\n- **Agrees with the source:**\n  - The test's only expected dependency is `Dependency::OutgoingEdges(1, (), edge_fingerprint(&graph, &[2]))`.\n  - `edge_fingerprint` in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/graph.rs` hashes only `graph.node_path` values of the targets. It never calls `Contents::fingerprint`.\n  - The `node_content` stub in the same impl panics, and the test's `ToolAgent` script calls only `outgoing_edges` and `submit_result`. So content fingerprinting is never legitimately reached.\n  - The `Contents` impl also panics in `fingerprint`, which guards against any unwanted content dependency.\n- **No redundancy:** The item carries no `{impl}` or `{test}` reference to the same target, so there is no redundant citation.",
